1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,167
The oldest man who ever lived
died the same year as the flood.

2
00:00:04,237 --> 00:00:05,430
Coincidence?

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,244
His name was Methuselah.

4
00:00:07,314 --> 00:00:10,020
He lived 969 years.

5
00:00:10,090 --> 00:00:13,321
His father, Enoch, "walked with God:

6
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:16,032
and he was not; for God took him."

7
00:00:16,102 --> 00:00:18,873
If you add up the ages in Genesis 5,

8
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:21,820
Methuselah's life
overlapped with Adam…

9
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:23,016
and with Noah.

10
00:00:23,086 --> 00:00:24,423
Now watch the math.

11
00:00:24,493 --> 00:00:28,883
Methuselah was 187 when
his son Lamech was born.

12
00:00:28,953 --> 00:00:32,342
Lamech was 182 when Noah was born.

13
00:00:32,412 --> 00:00:34,657
Noah was 600 when the flood came.

14
00:00:34,727 --> 00:00:42,066
187… plus 182… plus 600… equals 969.

15
00:00:42,136 --> 00:00:44,539
The exact year Methuselah died.

16
00:00:46,109 --> 00:00:49,227
Some say his name can
mean "when he dies,

17
00:00:49,267 --> 00:00:50,459
it shall be sent."

18
00:00:51,029 --> 00:00:55,234
But notice: the flood came the
same year his long life ended.

19
00:00:55,304 --> 00:00:58,351
As if God was waiting…
as long as He could.

20
00:00:58,421 --> 00:01:01,942
"The longsuffering of God
waited in the days of Noah,

21
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,956
while the ark was a preparing."

22
00:01:06,626 --> 00:01:08,489
And God is still waiting today.

23
00:01:08,559 --> 00:01:11,106
Not to punish you… but for you.

24
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:15,026
"The Lord is… not willing
that any should perish,

25
00:01:15,071 --> 00:01:17,566
but that all should
come to repentance."

26
00:01:17,636 --> 00:01:19,986
Coincidence… or God's timing?

27
00:01:20,056 --> 00:01:21,392
Comment one word.
